{"call_id":"call_SLF1GdRONSQPuCEiGSocMVie","process_id":"30904","turn_id":"019ca706-7f75-7c12-bec8-d13d46db3e96","command":["/usr/bin/bash","-lc","kspec task get @01KJDQ1EKVV4V60V7WT6DCK3H3 --json"],"cwd":"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"kspec task get @01KJDQ1EKVV4V60V7WT6DCK3H3 --json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1EKVV4V60V7WT6DCK3H3\",\n  \"slugs\": [],\n  \"title\": \"Triage promote action should optionally delete the inbox item after creating the task. Currently pro\",\n  \"type\": \"task\",\n  \"description\": \"Triage promote action should optionally delete the inbox item after creating the task. Currently promoted items stay in inbox requiring manual cleanup. Consider --consume flag or making deletion the default for promote (with snapshot preserved in triage record).\",\n  \"spec_ref\": \"@triage-cli-commands\",\n  \"status\": \"pending_review\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"context\": [],\n  \"priority\": 3,\n  \"tags\": [],\n  \"vcs_refs\": [],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:02.203Z\",\n  \"started_at\": \"2026-03-01T01:31:55.076Z\",\n  \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-01T01:31:56.326Z\",\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQAHM5SX18W9F5V0ET02G6\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:00.197Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: When `kspec triage act` executes a \\\"promote\\\" action, it creates a new task from the inbox item but leaves the original inbox item in the inbox. This requires a separate manual `kspec inbox delete` step to clean up, which is tedious and easy to forget. The inbox item's text is already preserved in the triage record's `item_snapshot` field, so the original is not needed for audit trail purposes.\\n\\n**Where**: \\n- `src/triage/actions.ts` lines 54-74 — the `promote` case in `executeTriageAction()`. Currently creates the task and returns, but never calls `deleteInboxItem()` for the promoted item.\\n- `src/cli/commands/triage.ts` lines 235-289 — the `triage act` command handler. This is where the `--consume` flag would be parsed and passed to `executeTriageAction()`.\\n- The `delete` and `duplicate` cases (lines 77-90, 117-130) already call `deleteInboxItem()` — the promote case can follow the same pattern.\\n\\n**How**: Two reasonable approaches:\\n1. **Flag approach**: Add `--consume` flag to `kspec triage act` that deletes the inbox item after promote. Pass it through `ExecuteTriageActionOptions` to `executeTriageAction()`.\\n2. **Default behavior**: Make deletion the default for promote (since the snapshot is preserved in the triage record), with a `--keep` flag to opt out.\\n\\nRecommendation: Option 2 (delete by default) is cleaner since every promoted item has its text preserved in `item_snapshot`. The `--keep` flag is the escape hatch. The `delete` and `duplicate` cases already delete inbox items as their default behavior, so promote doing the same is consistent.\\n\\nImplementation:\\n1. Add `consume` option to `ExecuteTriageActionOptions` (default true for promote)\\n2. In the `promote` case of `executeTriageAction()`, after creating the task, call `deleteInboxItem()` for `record.inbox_ref` unless consume is false\\n3. Add `--keep` flag to `kspec triage act` command that sets `consume: false`\\n4. Update dry-run output to mention deletion\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- `kspec triage act <ref>` on a promote record creates the task AND deletes the inbox item\\n- `kspec triage act <ref> --keep` creates the task but preserves the inbox item\\n- Dry-run output mentions that the inbox item would be deleted\\n- The `item_snapshot` in the triage record still contains the original text for audit trail\\n- Tests cover: promote with deletion (default), promote with --keep, dry-run output\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJKG7WFH1661Q65B70E3XAQF\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T01:29:39.569Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Execution context:\\n- Background: triage promote should consume inbox items by default while preserving audit snapshot in triage records.\\n- Scope: add default consume behavior for promote action, add --keep escape hatch, and update dry-run messaging/tests.\\n- Files: src/triage/actions.ts, src/cli/commands/triage.ts, triage CLI/action tests.\\n- Verification: targeted triage tests + kspec validate before submit.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJKGB939JWK2RT4H5M3WSB2S\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T01:31:30.793Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Implemented promote-consume behavior in shared triage action executor and triage CLI act command:\\n- Added promote consume control (default true) to executeTriageAction options.\\n- Promote now deletes referenced inbox item by default after task creation; --keep bypasses deletion.\\n- Dry-run now reports whether promoted inbox item would be deleted or kept.\\n- Added regression coverage in tests/triage-actions.test.ts and tests/triage-cli.test.ts for default consume, --keep, and dry-run messaging.\\nVerification:\\n- npm test -- tests/triage-actions.test.ts tests/triage-cli.test.ts (67 passed).\\n- kspec validate still fails with pre-existing project-wide meta/reference/alignment/completeness issues around observations slug/skill and unrelated alignment warnings.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJKGC61AKBA443BD79ERR95C\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T01:32:00.426Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Lifecycle note: this iteration inherited a stale KSPEC_SESSION_ID budget guard that blocked normal task start ('Task budget exhausted: 1/1'). Used one-shot env -u KSPEC_SESSION_ID for task start/submit transitions after code/test completion.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJKGCXACKNR9AS8J5240WSP1\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T01:32:24.268Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Opened PR #617: https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/617 (branch fix/triage-promote-consume-inbox). Task submitted to pending_review.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"todos\": [],\n  \"automation\": \"eligible\",\n  \"_sourceFile\": \"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\",\n  \"inherited_traits\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-json-output\",\n      \"title\": \"JSON Output Mode\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json flag is provided\",\n          \"then\": \"output is valid JSON with no ANSI color codes\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"output includes all data available in human-readable mode\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command encounters an error\",\n          \"then\": \"error is returned as JSON object with error field\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains references\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"references use @ prefix consistently\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"JSON output contains timestamps\",\n          \"when\": \"output is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"timestamps use ISO 8601 format\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports --json\",\n          \"when\": \"used with other formatting flags\",\n          \"then\": \"--json takes precedence over other format options\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-error-guidance\",\n      \"title\": \"Error Messages with Recovery Guidance\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes description of what went wrong\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters error\",\n          \"when\": \"error message is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"includes suggested action to resolve\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"reference not found\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"suggests checking ref with kspec search or kspec <type> list\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"invalid state transition\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates current state and valid next states\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"validation error\",\n          \"when\": \"error is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"indicates which field/value failed validation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"error in JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--json is active\",\n          \"then\": \"guidance included in structured error object\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-semantic-exit-codes\",\n      \"title\": \"Semantic Exit Codes\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command completes successfully\",\n          \"when\": \"operation succeeds\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 0\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters validation error\",\n          \"when\": \"user input is invalid\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"command is cancelled by user\",\n          \"when\": \"confirmation prompt declined\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"command encounters runtime error\",\n          \"when\": \"operation fails during execution\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"command finds nothing\",\n          \"when\": \"query returns no results\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 0 with empty result set\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"command used incorrectly\",\n          \"when\": \"invalid flags or arguments provided\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 1 with usage information\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"batch operation completes\",\n          \"when\": \"partial failures occur\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code 1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"command documentation\",\n          \"when\": \"developers implement commands\",\n          \"then\": \"exit code meanings documented in code\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-filterable-list\",\n      \"title\": \"Filterable List Commands\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"list command supports filtering\",\n          \"when\": \"--status <value> provided\",\n          \"then\": \"only items with matching status shown\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"list command supports filtering\",\n          \"when\": \"--tag <value> provided\",\n          \"then\": \"only items with matching tag shown\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"list command supports pagination\",\n          \"when\": \"--limit N provided\",\n          \"then\": \"output shows at most N items\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"list command supports pagination\",\n          \"when\": \"--offset N provided\",\n          \"then\": \"output skips first N items\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"multiple filters provided\",\n          \"when\": \"--status X --tag Y used together\",\n          \"then\": \"output shows items matching all filters (AND logic)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"no items match filters\",\n          \"when\": \"list command executes\",\n          \"then\": \"empty list shown with informative message\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"list command output\",\n          \"when\": \"results are displayed\",\n          \"then\": \"summary shows total matching items and filter state\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"list command supports count mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--count flag is provided\",\n          \"then\": \"outputs only the total number of matching items as a plain integer (no item details); ignores --limit and --offset; in JSON mode outputs {\\\"count\\\": N}\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-shadow-commit\",\n      \"title\": \"Shadow Branch Auto-Commit\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command modifies state in shadow worktree\",\n          \"when\": \"save operation completes successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"git commit is created in shadow branch with semantic message\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"commit message is generated\",\n          \"then\": \"message follows pattern operation-colon-ref-short with optional detail\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow commit is created\",\n          \"when\": \"item reference is available\",\n          \"then\": \"commit message includes ULID prefix (8 chars) or primary slug\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow is not configured (no worktree)\",\n          \"when\": \"command that would normally commit runs\",\n          \"then\": \"command completes successfully without attempting git operations\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"save operation fails\",\n          \"when\": \"validation or IO error occurs\",\n          \"then\": \"no commit is attempted and error is returned\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"shadow has remote configured\",\n          \"when\": \"commit succeeds\",\n          \"then\": \"push is attempted in fire-and-forget mode (failure doesn't block command)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-7\",\n          \"given\": \"commit or push fails\",\n          \"when\": \"save succeeded but git operation failed\",\n          \"then\": \"command succeeds but outputs warning about sync state\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-8\",\n          \"given\": \"command performs multiple related saves\",\n          \"when\": \"all saves complete successfully\",\n          \"then\": \"single atomic commit covers all changes\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@trait-dry-run\",\n      \"title\": \"Dry Run Preview Mode\",\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-1\",\n          \"given\": \"command supports dry run\",\n          \"when\": \"--dry-run flag is provided\",\n          \"then\": \"show what would be changed without applying\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-2\",\n          \"given\": \"dry run mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command completes\",\n          \"then\": \"no files are modified\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-3\",\n          \"given\": \"dry run mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"output is shown\",\n          \"then\": \"clear indication that this is a preview\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-4\",\n          \"given\": \"dry run mode is active\",\n          \"when\": \"command would error\",\n          \"then\": \"error shown but no state changed\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-5\",\n          \"given\": \"--dry-run and --force both provided\",\n          \"when\": \"command executes\",\n          \"then\": \"dry run takes precedence (no changes made)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ac-6\",\n          \"given\": \"dry run in JSON mode\",\n          \"when\": \"--dry-run --json provided\",\n          \"then\": \"JSON output includes dry_run boolean field\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQ1EKVV4V60V7WT6DCK3H3\",\n  \"slugs\": [],\n  \"title\": \"Triage promote action should optionally delete the inbox item after creating the task. Currently pro\",\n  \"type\": \"task\",\n  \"description\": \"Triage promote action should optionally delete the inbox item after creating the task. Currently promoted items stay in inbox requiring manual cleanup. Consider --consume flag or making deletion the default for promote (with snapshot preserved in triage record).\",\n  \"spec_ref\": \"@triage-cli-commands\",\n  \"status\": \"pending_review\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"depends_on\": [],\n  \"context\": [],\n  \"priority\": 3,\n  \"tags\": [],\n  \"vcs_refs\": [],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:33:02.203Z\",\n  \"started_at\": \"2026-03-01T01:31:55.076Z\",\n  \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-01T01:31:56.326Z\",\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJDQAHM5SX18W9F5V0ET02G6\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-26T19:38:00.197Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: When `kspec triage act` executes a \\\"promote\\\" action, it creates a new task from the inbox item but leaves the original inbox item in the inbox. This requires a separate manual `kspec inbox delete` step to clean up, which is tedious and easy to forget. The inbox item's text is already preserved in the triage record's `item_snapshot` field, so the original is not needed for audit trail purposes.\\n\\n**Where**: \\n- `src/triage/actions.ts` lines 54-74 — the `promote` case in `executeTriageAction()`. Currently creates the task and returns, but never calls `deleteInboxItem()` for the promoted item.\\n- `src/cli/commands/triage.ts` lines 235-289 — the `triage act` command handler. This is where the `--consume` flag would be parsed and passed to `executeTriageAction()`.\\n- The `delete` and `duplicate` cases (lines 77-90, 117-130) already call `deleteInboxItem()` — the promote case can follow the same pattern.\\n\\n**How**: Two reasonable approaches:\\n1. **Flag approach**: Add `--consume` flag to `kspec triage act` that deletes the inbox item after promote. Pass it through `ExecuteTriageActionOptions` to `executeTriageAction()`.\\n2. **Default behavior**: Make deletion the default for promote (since the snapshot is preserved in the triage record), with a `--keep` flag to opt out.\\n\\nRecommendation: Option 2 (delete by default) is cleaner since every promoted item has its text preserved in `item_snapshot`. The `--keep` flag is the escape hatch. The `delete` and `duplicate` cases already delete inbox items as their default behavior, so promote doing the same is consistent.\\n\\nImplementation:\\n1. Add `consume` option to `ExecuteTriageActionOptions` (default true for promote)\\n2. In the `promote` case of `executeTriageAction()`, after creating the task, call `deleteInboxItem()` for `record.inbox_ref` unless consume is false\\n3. Add `--keep` flag to `kspec triage act` command that sets `consume: false`\\n4. Update dry-run output to mention deletion\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- `kspec triage act <ref>` on a promote record creates the task AND deletes the inbox item\\n- `kspec triage act <ref> --keep` creates the task but preserves the inbox item\\n- Dry-run output mentions that the inbox item would be deleted\\n- The `item_snapshot` in the triage record still contains the original text for audit trail\\n- Tests cover: promote with deletion (default), promote with --keep, dry-run output\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJKG7WFH1661Q65B70E3XAQF\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T01:29:39.569Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Execution context:\\n- Background: triage promote should consume inbox items by default while preserving audit snapshot in triage records.\\n- Scope: add default consume behavior for promote action, add --keep escape hatch, and update dry-run messaging/tests.\\n- Files: src/triage/actions.ts, src/cli/commands/triage.ts, triage CLI/action tests.\\n- Verification: targeted triage tests + kspec validate before submit.\",\n      \"supersedes\": null,\n      \"superseded\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"_ulid\": \"01KJKGB939JWK2RT4H5M3WSB2S\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T01:31:30.793Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Implemented promote-consume behavior in shared triage action executor and triage CLI act command:\\n- Added promote consume control (default true) to executeTriageAction options.\\n- Promote now deletes referenced inbox item by default after task creation; --keep bypasses deletion.\\n- Dry-run now reports whether promoted inbox item would be deleted or kept.\\n- Added regression coverage in tests/triage-actions.test.ts and tests/triage-cli.test.ts for default consume, --keep, and dry-run messaging.\\nVerification: